  ;; aiueos-6600hs-1 -- the box that used to be the tailnet node `ubuntu-server`,
  ;; reinstalled 2026-09-16 (Ubuntu 24.04.4). The name is the owner's; the
  ;; hardware is NOT a 6600HS: Ryzen 5 7500F (6C/12T, no iGPU), 15 GiB DDR5,
  ;; and an ASRock Intel Arc **BMG G31** (PCI 8086:e223, 32 GiB VRAM). The GA
  ;; 6.8 kernel has no xe id for e223; the HWE 7.0.0-31 kernel binds it and
  ;; Mesa 25.2.8 ANV exposes it as Vulkan 1.4 with KHR_coopmat (fp16 1, bf16 1,
  ;; int dot 1). Tailscale SSH policy admits root@ only (same as k16/xavier).
  ;; Same llama.cpp build as k16 (llama-b10883 Vulkan, rsync'd from k16) and
  ;; the same /opt/murakumo join scripts + /etc/murakumo/join.env.
  ;;
  ;; Serves BOTH orcarouter models at once (units in deploy/systemd/
  ;; murakumo-6600hs1-{qwen38u,nex-n25-mini}-{llama,join}.service):
  ;;   :8097 qwen3.8-27b-uncensored  Q4_K_M + f16 mmproj, -ngl 99, ctx 8192 q8_0 KV
  ;;   :8090 nex-n2.5-mini-uncensored IQ4_XS + F16 mmproj, -ngl 999 --n-cpu-moe 20, ctx 65536
  ;; Why that split: weights are 15.65 + 17.43 GiB, so both cannot be fully
  ;; resident in 32 GiB. Measured 2026-09-16 (llama-bench -p 512 -n 128 -fa 1
  ;; -r 3, tok/s):
  ;;   Qwen alone -ngl 99 ............ pp512 407.1  tg128 11.62
  ;;   Nex  alone -ngl 99 ............ pp512 908.0  tg128 50.11
  ;;   Nex resident, Qwen -ngl 36/40 . pp512 297/307 tg128 3.36/3.50  (rejected)
  ;;   Qwen resident, Nex n-cpu-moe 24 pp512 200.7  tg128 25.2
  ;;   Qwen resident, Nex n-cpu-moe 20 pp512 139.7  tg128 27.6   (chosen)
  ;; E2E llama-server streaming (256 max_tokens, temp 0): Nex 20.4 tok/s TTFT
  ;; 0.40 s; Qwen 10.7 tok/s TTFT 0.47 s; both at once 15.4 / 9.3, 0 DeviceLost,
  ;; VRAM budget left 2.96 GiB. Through api.murakumo.cloud a 400-token qwen
  ;; job took 61.8 s wall (node-side 38.3 s = 10.77 tok/s decode) vs 175-267 s
  ;; on k16. Compare k16 qwen38u decode 2.5 and xavier nex decode 18.3.
  ;;
  ;; Routing today: qwen38u jobs come through the edge queue (this node and
  ;; k16 race; the gateway's soft cache-affinity sends a repeated prompt back
  ;; to whoever served it, so identical probes all landed on k16 -- probe with
  ;; distinct prompts). nex: since 2026-09-18 cloud-murakumo-api routes the id
  ;; by name to THIS node first over the Workers-VPC binding
  ;; MURAKUMO_6600HS1_PRIVATE (VPC service murakumo-6600hs1-chat, 192.168.1.2:8090
  ;; over the gad tunnel; x-murakumo-route-head: 6600hs1), xavier only when this
  ;; node is unreachable (cloud-murakumo-api PR #272, deploy de109263). The nex
  ;; join here is still enrolled in the edge queue but nex never flows through
  ;; the queue, so it stays idle by design. --poll-ms 250
  ;; on both joins (k16 polls at 1000). GuC firmware is 70.44.1 where 70.54.0
  ;; is recommended (Ubuntu linux-firmware 20240318) -- not measured as a
  ;; cost. Root ADR adr-2609161500.
  ;;
  ;; 2026-09-16 (later): THIS BOX WAS b70. deploy/systemd/murakumo-b70-llama.service
  ;; names jun@100.119.10.43 / hostname ubuntu-server -- the same machine before
  ;; the reinstall -- and that head led the murakumo-main pool (SYCL build,
  ;; stock Qwen3.8-27B Q4_K_M, --spec-type draft-mtp, decode 16.8-28 tok/s,
  ;; 2 slots x 32768). The reinstall removed the SYCL build, the stock weights,
  ;; the cloudflared tunnel behind MURAKUMO_B70_PRIVATE and the b70 join, so
  ;; /ready now reports pool-available {gad 0, b70 0, xavier 0} and a
  ;; model=murakumo-main request hung 120 s (http 000). Nothing here restores
  ;; that role: the uncensored 27B is not the stock model the pool probe
  ;; asserts, and stock + uncensored + Nex do not fit 32 GiB. Owner decision.
  ;; What was carried over: the same MTP speculative flags on the Vulkan build
  ;; lift qwen38u here from 10.7 to 17.2-18.0 tok/s E2E (2 slots x 16384,
  ;; q8_0 KV, default batch; VRAM budget left beside Nex ~857 MiB).
  ;;
  ;; 2026-09-16 (owner: "nex だけにして ok"): Qwen3.8 dropped from this box, so
  ;; the one-model rule holds without an exception. The qwen38u units stay on
  ;; the box DISABLED with their weights (same rollback convention as xavier's
  ;; murakumo-xavier-qwen38.service); their deploy/systemd copies are removed.
  ;; Nex has the whole card: -ngl 999. 2026-09-16: 2 slots x 65536, E2E 60.3 /
  ;; 58.8 tok/s single, 48.2 + 48.2 with both slots busy, 6291-token prompt
  ;; prefill 831 tok/s / decode 49.1, VRAM budget left 9.45 GiB.
  ;; 2026-09-18 (owner: "最大 toks, concurrency を 6600hs-1 で計測して"), 256-token
  ;; generations, temp 0.7, N concurrent, llama-server timings:
  ;;   --parallel 2  x 65536: N=1 60.6 | N=2 48.7+49.3 (aggregate 91)
  ;;   --parallel 4  x 65536: N=4 ~35 each (aggregate 128) | N=8 queued, same aggregate
  ;;   --parallel 6  x 65536: N=6 23.5 each (aggregate 131) | N=12 24.2 each (135)
  ;;   --parallel 8  x 65536: N=8 18.1 each (aggregate 137) | N=16 18.4 each (132)
  ;;   --parallel 16 x 32768: N=16 4.7 each (aggregate 73)  -- collapses, do not ship
  ;; Ceiling ~130-137 tok/s aggregate from 4 slots up; shipped --parallel 4 x
  ;; 65536 (--ctx-size 262144, --host 0.0.0.0 so the LAN binding reaches it)
  ;; so every admitted stream keeps >= 35 tok/s (xavier's single slot: 18.5).
  ;; The b70 role (murakumo-main) is NOT restored by this; see the paragraph
  ;; above and root ADR adr-2609161500 / adr-2609181200.
  {:name "aiueos-6600hs-1" :host "root@100.98.24.37" :rpc-ip "192.168.1.2" :mac "9c:6b:00:cf:ad:55" :roles ["compute"] :labels {:tier "gpu" :zone "jp" :role "vulkan-infer"} :node/serves "nex-n2.5-mini-uncensored"}]}
